<!---
An authoring aid, not part of the site: a link straight to the post's generated
story image, so it can be opened and saved without working out its URL.

Whether to render it at all is the caller's decision — post.webc only includes
it outside the live site. See src/_data/env.js.
--->
<aside webc:root="override">
    <a :href="socialImageUrl(slug, 'story')" target="_blank">Story image ↗</a>
</aside>

<style webc:scoped="story-image-link">
    :host {
        margin-top: var(--line-height-base);
        font-size: .8em;
        color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }

    :host::before {
        content: "Preview build";
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .05em;
        border: 1px dashed var(--color-text-muted);
        border-radius: 2px;
        padding: .1em .3em;
        margin-right: 1ch;
    }
</style>
